WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:12.100
82. Wind power. Around the world, people are looking for new, longer-lasting sources

2
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:19.060
of energy. One of these sources is the wind. Wind power has the potential to be an important

3
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:26.580
new way to create electricity. Wind power really is clean. Using wind turbines to generate

4
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:33.660
electricity creates no air pollution and requires no fuel. Using more wind power would actually

5
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:40.460
reduce pollution, as we would use less power from polluting sources. Besides, wind is free.

6
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:47.900
Building a turbine or mill costs money, but the wind itself costs nothing. In addition to being

7
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:53.980
free, wind is sustainable. We won't run out of wind the way we will run out of coal, oil, or other

8
00:00:53.980 --> 00:01:01.020
fuel sources. In fact, the power wind can create is much greater than the world's current energy

9
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:07.740
needs, and the power can help people or small communities be self-reliant. They would rely only

10
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:15.660
on their turbine, not a city power grid. However, even wind power has some drawbacks. Some people

11
00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:21.980
find wind turbines ugly. They think the turbines ruin the landscape. The turbines can also be quite

12
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:28.380
loud, which is a problem for people and animals nearby. The turbines may affect animals more than

13
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:34.700
people. They can disrupt birds' flight patterns. What's worse, they may frighten other animals away

14
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:41.980
from the area. The turbines can also cause problems with TV signals. The key to making wind power work

15
00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:48.300
seems to be building more and better turbines. If we do that, it seems likely that wind power

16
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.100
will be more and more important in our future.
